.git
.github
.agents
.codex
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.cache
.docker-data
.pytest_cache
.run
.venv*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/.pixi
**/node_modules
mkdocs/site
ui/dist
runs
logs
tests/results
tests/deepeval/results
papers
splash_links/links.sqlite
# Tiled catalog databases (and SQLite sidecars) are runtime state, not image
# content. Docker Tiled keeps its catalog in the tiled_data volume. Only a
# future :local image target may bundle a local catalog (H0 escalation E3).
**/tiled_catalog*.db
**/tiled_catalog*.db-*
# Source-RAG indexes hold paper-text chunks; mount them at runtime and point
# HYBRID_RAG_LITERATURE_INDEX / HYBRID_RAG_OPS_INDEX at them (H0 escalation E4).
storage/source_index
# T24B backstops. The Dockerfile copies an allowlist; these keep private or runtime data
# out of the build context even if a COPY line is widened by mistake.
**/.env
**/*.pdf
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/source_index
storage/artifacts
storage/parsed
storage/crops
storage/state
# Stale developer copy of app/modules/kg_rag_api.py (ROUTE_POLICIES R26-R31: "not packaged";
# AUD-02). It is retired under T17B; until then the images' COPY scripts/ must not ship it.
scripts/app

# graphify output and caches (local analysis only)
**/graphify-out

# T24E: Ansible handoff and host tools are never image content.
deploy

# T26A (owner O-R1 Q2): adopted releases keep a nested storage/kg/<corpus>/v<N>/graph.json that is a byte
# copy of the flat file. The flat copies stay the byte source in images (release_contract.md section 7), so the
# nested graph copies are not sent to the build context (they would duplicate ~220 MB). manifest.json and
# validation.json stay in the context. Git stores one blob either way. (E3 errata, applied 2026-11-06: KG JSON
# otherwise ships with the image; baking never selects data, release_contract.md section 7.)
storage/kg/*/v*/graph.json
